      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In cases where the morphology leans towards a more unusual or atypical presentation, the L-series codes may not capture the full complexity. When the clinical notes describe the morphology as \"erratic\" or \"gnarly\", it may suggest a more structured approach. Consider consulting with pathologists, dermatologists, or medical directors for guidance on coding unusual presentations. For extreme cases, consider consulting the ICD-10 \"Unspecified\" codes or even requesting a pathology review, but still document the clinical characteristics thoroughly in the medical record to ensure a clear rationale for the chosen code.",
